cription":"There are 23 five-star players in the class, and we scout each one's game for the next level.","published":"2026-11-27T17:00:30.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/recruiting/story/_/id/48543549/college-football-recruiting-2027-prospects-five-star-scouts-take","type":"Story","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Which teams have the best odds to make the College Football Playoff?","description":"We are tracking the odds for making the CFP, earning a bye and winning it all.","published":"2026-11-27T15:51:28.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50532919/college-football-playoff-odds-predictions","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN staff","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Houston, rivalry color rushes lead top uniforms of CFB Week 13","description":"Just because it's rivalry week doesn't mean teams still can't put their best foot forward with uniform swag.","published":"2026-11-27T15:00:13.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50598211/college-football-uniforms-week-13-houston","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN staff","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"What the world looked like the last time Texas A&M beat Texas","description":"It has been 15 years since Texas A&M came out on top on the gridiron against its rivals to the southwest.","published":"2026-11-27T17:36:28.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/47109982/texas-aggies-lone-star-showdown-last-win-2010","type":"Story","byline":"J.J. Post","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"2027 NFL draft Big Board rankings: Mel Kiper's top 25 prospects, best by position","description":"Three quarterbacks who could go early? Big changes in the rankings? Mel Kiper Jr. stacks the best players on the 2027 draft board as of late November.","published":"2026-11-27T14:49:00.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/draft2027/story/_/id/50182998/2027-nfl-draft-rankings-kiper-big-board-top-prospects","type":"Story","byline":"Mel Kiper Jr.","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"What are the conference title game clinching scenarios in Week 13?","description":"Plenty of spots are still up for grabs entering the final week of the regular season.","published":"2026-11-27T12:39:26.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50583399/conference-title-game-clinching-scenarios-week-13","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN","source":"ESPN"}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5082149/clev-lubin","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Clev_Lubin"},"pick":{"pick":53,"round":2,"team":"LAR","provisional":true},"wiki":{"rules":4,"title":"Clev Lubin","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Clev_Lubin","description":"American football player","touched":"2026-11-22T04:18:06Z","intro":"Clevmer Lubin (CLEV-mah LOO-bin) is an American college football defensive end for the Louisville Cardinals. He previously played for the Army Black Knights, Iowa Western Reivers, and Coastal Carolina Chanticleers.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"Lubin played football and basketball for Suffern High School and was considered one of the best players the school has produced. He played as both a defensive end and running back, and during his senior season he recorded 1,053 rushing yards and 16 touchdowns on 110 carries. He also set a program record of 1,062 rushing yards during the 2019 season. Due to his success on the field, he was named the Gatorade New York State Player of the Year as a senior and was also named The Journal News Rockland County Football Player of the Year. Lubin received several Division I offers, and on December 14, 2020, he committed to play at Army. Following his senior season, Lubin spent a year prepping at USMAPS before joining the Black Knights in 2022."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"ARMY\nAfter joining the Black Knights, Lubin did not see any game action his true freshman season and transferred to Iowa Western.\n\nIOWA WESTERN\nWhile at Iowa Western, Lubin helped lead the team to the NJCAA D1 Football National Championship. Following the season he was named a first-team NJCAA All-American.\n\nCOASTAL CAROLINA\nOn July 1, 2024, Lubin enrolled at Coastal Carolina. In 10 games, he finished 16th nationally in sacks and contributed 12.5 tackles for loss. Following the season, he was given First-Team All-Sun Belt honors.\nAfter the season, Lubin again entered the transfer portal.\n\nLOUISVILLE\nOn December 21, 2024, Lubin committed to Louisville. On January 2, 2026, Lubin announced he would return to Louisville for another season."}]}}